<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of Chioggia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1378">1378</a>–<a href="/years/1381">1381</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chioggia">Chioggia</a> (1378–1381) was a war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquileia">Aquileia</a> among Genoa's allies. In 1379 a Genoese fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietro-doria">Pietro Doria</a> seized Chioggia at the edge of the Venetian lagoon, but the Venetians blockaded it there and forced its surrender in 1380. The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> of 1381 left neither side dominant, though Genoa never again seriously threatened Venice.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-chioggia.jpg" alt="War of Chioggia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canal_Vena_in_Chioggia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
